    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 14 St. Sylvester Villas is a most charming cottage-style residence, perfectly positioned in a mature and highly sought-after location just a short stroll from the gates of Malahide Castle and its magnificent grounds. Within easy walking distance of Malahide Village, residents can enjoy every imaginable convenience, from shops, schools, and churches to restaurants, boutiques, and the Dart station.\nSet in a quiet cul-de-sac, the property is surrounded by generous private gardens and bordered by mature hedgerows, offering both privacy and a wonderful sense of tranquillity. The traditional double-fronted façade makes a delightful first impression, while inside, the deceptively spacious accommodation includes an extended kitchen to the rear, an inviting entrance hall, a comfortable sitting room, three bedrooms, and a bathroom. Well maintained with triple and double glazed windows throughout, the property presents an exceptional opportunity for buyers in search of a forever home, whether downsizing, purchasing for the first time, or seeking a family residence with character.\nMalahide itself is a picturesque seaside village, renowned for its vibrant atmosphere, boutique shopping, and excellent restaurants. With the Dart providing swift access to the city centre and beyond, and a wide range of sporting and leisure facilities nearby, from GAA and rugby to tennis, cricket, and hockey, the location caters to every lifestyle. For those who love the outdoors, peaceful walks through Malahide Castle's grounds or along the scenic coastline are just moments away."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 3.60m x 1.02m\nCarpet flooring, high ceilings\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.60m x 3.00m\nCarpet flooring, built in wadrobes, triple glazed window to front\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.01m x 3.53m\nBuilt in wardrobe, double glazed windows\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.55m x 2.40m\nCarpet flooring, double glazed windows\n\nFamily Bathroom - 2.45m x 1.50m\nFully tiled bathroom comprising shower, heated towel rail, hand wash basin and wc\n\nLiving Room - 4.29m x 3.91m\nFireplace, triple glazed window to front, carpet flooring\n\nDining room - 3.05m x 2.48m\nCarpet flooring, double glazed window to rear\n\nUtillity Room - 3.00m x 2.05m\nAmple storage space, dryer, access to kitchen and separate door to front\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room - 5.26m x 2.32m\nFitted kitchen with ample floor and wall units, oven and hob, extractor, sink unit, plumbed for washing machine, double glazed window, door to rear garden\n\n"
      },
